---
description: Shared NextForge engineering rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` before changing code. `CLAUDE.md` and `.github/copilot-instructions.md` mirror the same project contract for other agents.

- Use the existing Next.js App Router, strict TypeScript, and feature-based structure.
- Keep route handlers thin; put reusable infrastructure in `lib/` and domain behavior in `features/<domain>/`.
- Keep server-only code and secrets out of client components.
- Reuse existing API clients, auth session helpers, query patterns, and UI components.
- Do not introduce a new library or abstraction when an existing local pattern solves the problem.
- For behavior changes, add or update focused tests when the repository has a test harness.
- Validate changes with `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and `pnpm build`.
- Never edit files or execute commands on behalf of a user without explicit approval.
